    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265">

                <pb facs="0311" n="1145" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 103.96/324</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-06T23:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 6, 1918—11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 6, 6.52 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8928. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]:</p>
                <p>No. 238. Our 157. At a meeting today with the British, French, and Italians, the
                    proposed draft was considered satisfactory as a whole. I am sending a separate
                    cable with a few suggestions which it is hoped may be incorporated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
